# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every line here has a reason. If you cannot state the reason, delete the line:
# an unexplained ignore rule is how a file that matters goes missing for a year.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build output. Cargo's target/ grows to several GB and is a pure function of
# the source; committing it would be storing a derived artifact.
/target/
**/target/

# Dependency lockfiles are NOT ignored. Cargo.lock is committed, for two
# reasons: this project ships binaries (a library would not need it), and a
# lockfile is the only record of the exact versions a build was verified
# against. Ignoring it means "it built last Tuesday" stops being reproducible.

# Runtime state produced by the tool itself: tokens, logs, job output.
# Secrets must never enter history -- a committed token has to be rotated, not
# deleted, because history keeps it.
token.txt
config.json
*.local
*.local.*
.env
*.log

# Release artifacts. These are outputs of a build, not sources. Ship them as
# release assets, never as repository content: a dozen 13 MB zips is 150 MB of
# dead weight that every clone pays for.
/dist/
*.zip

# Editor and OS debris. Personal, machine-specific, no information for anyone else.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python leftovers (this repo may grow helper scripts).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
